    description:
      '🔥 Day 8: What is Spring Container?\n\nThe Spring Container is the heart of the Spring Framework ❤️\nWithout the Spring Container, concepts like IoC and Dependency Injection wouldn\'t work.\n\n🔹 What is Spring Container?\n👉 Definition: Spring Container is the core component of Spring Framework that creates, manages, configures, and destroys objects (Beans).\nSimply put:\n✔ Creates objects\n✔ Injects dependencies\n✔ Manages bean lifecycle\n✔ Handles configuration\n\n🔥 How Spring Container Works?\nApplication Starts\n ↓\nSpring Container Created\n ↓\nScans Components\n ↓\nCreates Beans\n ↓\nInjects Dependencies\n ↓\nApplication Ready\n\n🔹 Types of Spring Containers\n1️⃣ BeanFactory\nBasic container.\nBeanFactory factory;\n✔ Lightweight\n✔ Lazy initialization\n2️⃣ ApplicationContext (Most Used)\nApplicationContext context;\n✔ Advanced features\n✔ Event handling\n✔ Bean management\n✔ Internationalization\n\n🔹 Real-Life Analogy\n🏭 Factory Manager\nWithout manager:\nWorkers arrange everything manually.\nWith manager:\nManager assigns work automatically.\n\n👉 Spring Container acts as the manager.\n\n🔹 Responsibilities of Spring Container\n✔ Create beans\n✔ Manage bean lifecycle\n✔ Inject dependencies\n✔ Configure objects\n✔ Handle scopes\n\n🔥 Spring Container + IoC + DI\nSpring Container\n ↓\nImplements IoC\n ↓\nUses Dependency Injection\n\n🔹 Why Spring Container is Important?\n✔ Loose coupling\n✔ Better testing\n✔ Easy maintenance\n✔ Automatic dependency management\n✔ Cleaner architecture\n\n🔥 Interview Question\nQ: What is Spring Container?\n✅ Answer:\n"Spring Container is the core component of Spring Framework that creates, configures, manages, and injects dependencies into Spring Beans."\n\n💡 Pro Tip:\nWhenever you use @Component, @Service, @Repository, or @Controller, Spring Container creates and manages those objects automatically 🚀\n\n📌 Final Thought:\n"Spring Container is the brain of Spring Framework, responsible for managing the entire lifecycle of application objects."',
