    description:
      '🔥 Day 11: Bean Lifecycle Overview (High Level)\n\nUnderstanding the Bean Lifecycle helps you know what Spring does behind the scenes when creating and managing objects 🚀\nEvery Spring Bean goes through a lifecycle from creation to destruction.\n\n🔹 What is Bean Lifecycle?\n👉 Definition: Bean Lifecycle is the sequence of steps a Spring Bean follows from creation to destruction.\nCreate Bean\n ↓\nInject Dependencies\n ↓\nInitialize Bean\n ↓\nReady to Use\n ↓\nDestroy Bean\n\n🔥 Why is Bean Lifecycle Important?\n✔ Understand Spring Internals\n✔ Better Resource Management\n✔ Initialize objects properly\n✔ Clean up resources before shutdown\n\n🔥 High-Level Bean Lifecycle Flow\nApplication Starts\n ↓\nSpring Container Created\n ↓\nBean Instantiated\n ↓\nDependencies Injected\n ↓\nBean Initialized\n ↓\nBean Ready for Use\n ↓\nApplication Stops\n ↓\nBean Destroyed\n\n🔹 Lifecycle Visualization\nConstructor\n ↓\nDependency Injection\n ↓\n@PostConstruct\n ↓\nBean Usage\n ↓\n@PreDestroy\n\n🔹 Real-Life Analogy\n🏢 Employee Lifecycle\nHire Employee\n ↓\nProvide Training\n ↓\nEmployee Works\n ↓\nRetirement\n\nSpring Bean lifecycle works similarly.\n\n🔥 Important Annotations\nAnnotationPurpose@ComponentCreate Bean@AutowiredInject Dependency@PostConstructInitialization@PreDestroyCleanup Before Destruction\n\n🔥 Interview Question\nQ: What are the major phases of the Spring Bean Lifecycle?\n✅ Answer:\nBean Instantiation\nDependency Injection\nInitialization\nReady for Use\nBean Destruction\n\n💡 Pro Tip:\nFor interviews, remember this sequence:\nCreate → Inject → Initialize → Use → Destroy 🚀\n\n📌 Final Thought:\n"A Spring Bean doesn\'t just get created—it follows a complete lifecycle managed by the Spring Container."',
