    title: "What is Spring Boot?",
    image: "public/Spring/Day_61.png",
    description:
      "🔥 Day 61: What is Spring Boot?\n\nImagine you're building a REST API using the traditional Spring Framework.\nBefore writing a single line of business logic, you need to:\n❌ Configure XML or Java Config\n❌ Set up Tomcat\n❌ Configure database connections\n❌ Add multiple dependencies\n❌ Configure logging\n❌ Set up component scanning\n\nThat's a lot of setup! 😓\n👉 Spring Boot solves all of these problems by making Spring development faster and easier. 🚀\n\n🔹 What is Spring Boot?\n👉 Spring Boot is an extension of the Spring Framework that simplifies the development of Spring applications.\nIt provides:\n✅ Auto Configuration\n✅ Embedded Servers\n✅ Starter Dependencies\n✅ Production-ready features\n\nSo you can focus on writing business logic instead of configuration.\n🔥 Why Do We Need Spring Boot?\nTraditional Spring:\n❌ Lots of configuration\n❌ Manual dependency management\n❌ External web server setup\n❌ Longer development time\n\nSpring Boot:\n✅ Minimal configuration\n✅ Faster development\n✅ Embedded server\n✅ Ready-to-run applications\n\n🔥 Spring Boot Architecture\nDeveloper\n ↓\nSpring Boot\n ↓\nAuto Configuration\n ↓\nEmbedded Server\n ↓\nSpring Application\n\n🔹 Real-Life Analogy\n🏠 Buying a House\nTraditional Spring\nBuy Land\n↓\nBuild Foundation\n↓\nConstruct House\n↓\nInstall Utilities\n↓\nMove In\nYou handle every step yourself.\nSpring Boot\nBuy Ready House\n↓\nMove In\n\n🔥 Best Practices\n✅ Use Spring Boot Starters instead of adding individual dependencies.\n✅ Keep the @SpringBootApplication class in the root package so component scanning works as expected.\n✅ Store configuration in application.properties or application.yml.\n✅ Use Spring Boot Actuator for monitoring production applications.\n\n🔥 Interview Question\nQ: What is Spring Boot, and how is it different from the Spring Framework?\n✅ Answer:\nSpring Boot is an extension of the Spring Framework that simplifies application development through features such as auto-configuration, starter dependencies, embedded servers, and production-ready tools. While the Spring Framework provides the core infrastructure, Spring Boot reduces configuration and helps developers build and deploy Spring applications much faster.\n\n💡 Pro Tip:\nRemember these four keywords for interviews:\n✅ Auto Configuration\n✅ Starter Dependencies\n✅ Embedded Server\n✅ Production-Ready\n\nAnd don't forget:\nSpring Boot is not a replacement for the Spring Framework—it is built on top of it to simplify development.\n📌 Final Thought:\n\"Spring Boot transformed Java development by removing unnecessary configuration and allowing developers to focus on solving business problems. With features like auto-configuration, embedded servers, and starter dependencies, it has become the go-to framework for building modern, scalable, and production-ready applications.\"",
