      "🚀 Day 81: REST API Introduction in Spring Boot\n\nToday I started learning one of the most important concepts in backend development — REST APIs with Spring Boot.\nI explored how Spring Boot makes it easier to build APIs that allow different applications and services to communicate with each other.\n\n🔹 What I learned today:\n• What is a REST API?\n• HTTP methods — GET, POST, PUT, DELETE\n• Understanding endpoints and URLs\n• @RestController\n• @GetMapping and @PostMapping\n• How requests and responses work\n• Returning data from a Spring Boot API\n\nOne thing I’m realizing throughout this journey is that building an API is not just about writing code — it’s about designing a clean way for systems to communicate.\n\nStill learning. Still building. 💻🔥\n📌 Day 81 of my Backend Development Journey",
